      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "SAME ACTION, DIFFERENT ALTITUDE:",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "eAEWBf2C",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2010,
      "y": 1070,
      "width": 1060,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 298137863,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1105240494,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Verb: To eat / To go / To do\n\nPLAIN:\n  taberu / iku / suru\n  tabeta? (Did you eat? - casual)\n\nPOLITE (teinei-go):\n  tabemasu / ikimasu / shimasu\n  tabemashita ka? (Did you eat? - polite)\n  Rule: ichidan ru -> masu, godan u -> imasu\n\nKEIGO - Two directions:\n\nSONKEIGO (Respectful - raise OTHER person):\n  Other person eats: meshiagaru (not taberu)\n  Other person goes: irassharu (not iku)\n  Kyaku-sama ga meshiagaru (Customer eats - honored)\n\nKENJOUGO (Humble - lower SELF):\n  I eat (humble): itadaku (instead of taberu)\n  I go (humble): mairu (instead of iku)\n  Watashi ga itadakimasu (I humbly eat)\n\nKEY: Change verb + use o/go prefix + change pronouns",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Verb: To eat / To go / To do\n\nPLAIN:\n  taberu / iku / suru\n  tabeta? (Did you eat? - casual)\n\nPOLITE (teinei-go):\n  tabemasu / ikimasu / shimasu\n  tabemashita ka? (Did you eat? - polite)\n  Rule: ichidan ru -> masu, godan u -> imasu\n\nKEIGO - Two directions:\n\nSONKEIGO (Respectful - raise OTHER person):\n  Other person eats: meshiagaru (not taberu)\n  Other person goes: irassharu (not iku)\n  Kyaku-sama ga meshiagaru (Customer eats - honored)\n\nKENJOUGO (Humble - lower SELF):\n  I eat (humble): itadaku (instead of taberu)\n  I go (humble): mairu (instead of iku)\n  Watashi ga itadakimasu (I humbly eat)\n\nKEY: Change verb + use o/go prefix + change pronouns",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
